# ArchiveXL: the port's only manifest, next to its only archive (cyberpunkvrport.archive, which
# carries everything: player cameras and the optics catalogue, props, magazines, the basketball,
# the monowire material and the physical-crouch animgraph).
#
# WITHOUT THE FACTORIES THE ITEM ROUTE IS SILENTLY DEAD. An item whose `entityName` is a factory
# name -- Items.VRPortLoadOverture (the Overture's speedloader), Items.VRPortHlTest and
# Items.VRSmokeWheel (vr_smoke_wheel -> vrcigarette\vr_wheel.ent) -- resolves that name through a
# factory csv, and a name that resolves to nothing does not fail loudly: the game's
# `AddItemToSlot` returns TRUE and leaves the slot empty. Measured 2026-09-02: both items reported
# a successful attach and `GetItemInSlot` came back null.
#
# The csvs must stay COOKED C2dArrays (that is how mods\archive\build\base\vrport\vrp_props.csv
# is built): ArchiveXL reads a text csv as zero rows, logs "Loading factory", and the name again
# resolves to nothing.
#
# This file belongs next to cyberpunkvrport.archive in archive\pc\mod\.
factories:
  - base\vrport\vrp_props.csv
  - vrcigarette\vr_wheel.csv
